       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. A single 5 g dose can cause serious liver injury, and repeating it three times a day could be fatal. Normal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\nHere are some other ways to go ahead:\n- **Enter a dose in the safe range.** I can do this right now. Examples are 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum).\n- **Check for a typo or unit error.** If you meant 500 mg, or a weight-based dose of about 15 mg/kg (about 1000 mg for this patient), I can enter that.\n- **Ask pharmacy or toxicology.** If this is for an unusual situation, they can review it, and the order can go through your hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
